    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This is Act One - \"Behind the Sword\" of Episode 11 in the \"Sounds of Stanford\" PWR 2CG class, taught by Chris Gerben. It explores the narrator's experience with learning one of the oldest martial arts in the world, known as wushu. It is perhaps one of the most popular martial arts in China, yet it remains highly unknown in most of America, with the exception of kung fu movies. This part of the podcast will detail the narrator's first year experience with wushu as well as the often unseen component of competition as an individual and team sport. Includes interviews with Alex Wells, Delaney Sullivan, and Stanford Wushu team member Chris Bernedo. It also features sound clips from a Stanford Wushu practice as well as sounds from the 18th Collegiate Wushu competition.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
